---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// S4.3: honest placeholder terms — short, accurate, no fabricated boilerplate.
// Set LAST_UPDATED to the cutover date at launch (S4.4 runbook).
const LAST_UPDATED = '12 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Tunnex — Terms"
  description="Plain-language terms for using the tunnex.io website and pre-launch software."
>
  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:py-20">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Terms</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="rounded-md border border-l-4 border-warning/40 border-l-warning bg-warning/10 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-text"
      role="note"
    >
      <strong>Pre-launch document, pending legal review.</strong> These terms are deliberately short and
      honest. A full, lawyer-reviewed agreement will replace them before any paid transaction. We won't
      pretend to jurisdiction, arbitration, or liability language we haven't had drafted.
    </div>

    <div class="legal flex flex-col gap-6">
      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2>Using this site</h2>
        <p>
          You're welcome to read tunnex.io, join the waitlist, request a trial, and contact us.
          Please don't abuse the forms, attempt to break the site, or use it to send others
          unsolicited mail. We may rate-limit or block traffic that does.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2>Pre-launch software</h2>
        <p>
          Tunnex is in the run-up to its beta. Anything we describe here is offered as-is, with no
          warranty, while we're still building. Don't rely on pre-launch software for anything you
          can't afford to have break. When the beta ships, its own license terms apply to the
          software itself.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2>Our content and marks</h2>
        <p>
          The Tunnex name, logo, and the words and images on this site are ours. WireGuard® is a
          registered trademark of Jason A. Donenfeld. You can link to us and quote us fairly; please
          don't pass our brand off as your own.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We'll update these terms as Tunnex grows toward launch, and we'll replace them with a
          proper agreement before we charge anyone. The "last updated" date above tells you when
          they last changed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? <a href="mailto:support@tunnex.io">support@tunnex.io</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--t-text);
  }
  .legal :global(h2) {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .legal :global(a) {
    color: var(--t-link);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .legal :global(a:hover) {
    color: var(--t-link-hover);
  }
  .legal :global(p) {
    color: var(--t-text-muted);
  }
  .legal :global(strong) {
    color: var(--t-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
